      "finding_id": "plain:sqli:0",
      "cwe_id": "CWE-89",
      "explanation": "The `parse` method now returns `repr(query_expr.parseString(query)[0])` instead of generating parameterized SQL. The `repr` of the parsed query tree (e.g., `SearchTerm`, `SearchAnd`) contains the raw user-supplied search terms (e.g., `singleterm`, `phrase`, `regex`) directly in the string. In `utils.py`, this string is used as a SQL fragment (`query = [parser.parse(...)]`) and `qvars` is set to an empty dict. Consequently, user input is concatenated directly into the SQL query without parameterization, allowing SQL injection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "alerta/database/backends/postgres/queryparser.py",
          "lines": [
            181,
            184
          ],
          "source": null,
          "content": "def parse(self, query, default_field=None):\n        default_field = default_field or QueryParser.DEFAULT_FIELD\n        return repr(query_expr.parseString(query)[0]).replace('__default_field__', default_field)",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "alerta/database/backends/postgres/utils.py",
          "lines": [
            145,
            152
          ],
          "source": null,
          "content": "if params.get('q', None):\n            try:\n                parser = QueryParser()\n                query = [parser.parse(\n                    query=params['q'],\n                    default_field=params.get('q.df')\n                )]\n                qvars = dict()  # type: Dict[str, Any]",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": false
        }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Restore the `to_sql` methods that generate parameterized SQL queries and return the parameter dictionary. Ensure that `utils.py` passes these parameters to the database driver for safe execution.",
